WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:11.542
An inner equi-join pairs rows from two tables wherever their join keys test equal. Unmatched parent rows and NULL join keys evaluate to unknown under three-valued logic and are excluded from the output.

2
00:00:11.542 --> 00:00:23.391
For large unindexed joins, the engine builds an in-memory hash table on the smaller relation in O of M time, then streams the larger table through in O of N time, probing each key in constant time.

3
00:00:23.391 --> 00:00:35.693
Watch out for join fan-out! If an order has three line items and two payment attempts, joining both child tables directly produces six rows for one order, silently doubling or tripling your SUM totals.

4
00:00:35.693 --> 00:00:47.676
Eliminate fan-out by grouping each child table to the shared parent key inside a CTE before joining. When both sides have one row per order ID, every aggregate stays one hundred percent exact.
